[38;2;124;124;124mSwan theorem. So a "non-geometric" module is a $C^\infty(M)$-module that does [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mNOT arise as the module of sections of any vector bundle over $M$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mBy the Serre-Swan theorem, the geometric modules (sections of vector bundles) [0m
